### Deliverable D: Simulated Data Statement
##### Project Title: Real-Time Network Intrusion Detection System (NIDS)
**Team Identifier:**  Group 16 |  **Course:**  FUSE AI-201 Capstone
In compliance with FUSE AI-201 Module 6 portfolio requirements, Group 16 explicitly details the origin, nature, and usage of real versus simulated data within this project:

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

##### 1. Benchmark Dataset (Real Historical Telemetry)
The machine learning classifier, feature transformation pipeline (ColumnTransformer), and baseline performance evaluations are grounded entirely in authentic benchmark telemetry from the public  **NSL-KDD dataset** .
*   **Training Dataset (KDDTrain+.txt)** : Consists of 125,973 connection log records across 41 predictive attributes.
*   **Isolated Test Dataset (KDDTest+.txt)** : Consists of 22,544 independent connection records used for final model validation.
*   **Sample Inference File (sample_nsl_kdd_logs.csv)** : Extracted directly from NSL-KDD test logs to evaluate batch CSV parsing and single-connection UI forms within the Streamlit application.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

##### 2. Production Prediction Logs & Drift Simulation (Simulated Data Disclosure)
To satisfy Module 6 MLOps requirements for  **Production Monitoring (Sub-Module 6.6)**  and  **Data/Concept Drift Detection (Sub-Module 6.7)**  prior to live enterprise deployment:
*   **Prediction Log Database (predictions.db)** : We generated 21 days of synthetic inference request logs using an automated simulation script (simulate_logs.py). This logged input feature payloads, model confidence scores, status codes (including occasional 500 errors), and latency metrics.
*   **Synthetic Drift Insertion** : To verify that our monitoring dashboard and SciPy/Evidently AI drift detection alerts function correctly, a synthetic distribution shift (elevated host connection counts and altered protocol proportions) was intentionally planted in the final 6 days of the log history.
*   **Data Marking & Isolation** : Every synthetically generated record in SQLite is explicitly flagged with  **is_simulated = 1**  to prevent simulated monitoring data from polluting future real-world retraining pipelines.

